  "reason": "Evidence: The current best is config_010 (scvi_n200, vit_l, transformer, weighted) at 0.725 acc, with config_050 (same but concat) at 0.721 and config_020 (resnet50 instead of vit_l) at 0.713. All four scvi_n200+transformer combinations are tested, and the pattern is clear: scvi_n200 > pca_n2000 > scgpt, vit_l ≥ resnet50, transformer > avgpool, weighted ≥ concat. Question: config_041 (scvi_n200, vit_l, avgpool, weighted) is the closest untested variant to the best configuration, swapping only transformer→avgpool. It tests whether the ~3.5% transformer advantage seen with resnet50 (config_020 vs config_030) holds with vit_l, and whether avgpool could be a cheaper near-equivalent. Why this is the best use: With 1 experiment remaining after this, config_041 has the highest expected accuracy among all untested options (~0.69–0.71) while retaining all other optimal components. It is also expected to be relatively cheap (~3–4 GPU hours, comparable to config_010's 3.60 since vit_l configs train faster than resnet50 configs). If it underperforms as expected, it confirms transformer aggregation is necessary and solidifies config_010 as the final answer with high confidence, leaving the last experiment for a long-shot exploration if desired."
}

